here's an interesting story that has  some people on the left sort of upset or  or  certainly at least concerned on august  17th  about eight days ago the democratic  national committee  removed language from a draft platform  a draft document calling for an end to  subsidies  of fossil fuel companies  and the democratic national committee  and joe biden  and senator kamala harris historically  have opposed fossil fuel subsidies  they've said they would end them and it  was in a draft document  and yet eight days ago the call for the  end to these fossil fuel subsidies was  quietly removed  why did it happen it's not completely  clear but there was huge  backlash a lot of climate activists saw  it  as a stab in the back many people  alleged that  look this is joe biden he said he was  going to do one thing and then they  quietly remove it from the document and  now all of a sudden they're no longer  against abolishing fossil fuel  subsidies which cost somewhere between  20 and 650 billion dollars each year  depending on what you include and how  you measure it  and a bunch of people reacted by saying  this exposes the true biden biden  doesn't really want to do the things he  claims he wants to do  on climate or on whatever else and  uh it's it's sort of biden showing his  true colors  now after the backlash it's been added  back in  and again it has been restated that  joe biden and kamala harris and the dnc  support ending subsidies to fossil fuel  companies  and of course the reaction from many was  and it's not a crazy reaction  joe biden doesn't really support it but  he only got shamed back  into it right now so you could chalk  this up to confusion you could chalk it  up to a misunderstanding you could chalk  it up to bad faith  i have to tell you it seems unlikely to  me  that what happened here is that they  really were trying to just  remove this pledge to end fossil fuel  subsidies  and they got caught and they put it back  in the way the dnc operates is  if they want to back away from some kind  of promise they do it and they come up  with flowery or non-offensive language  to  to defend it so i actually think it's  more likely that this was some kind of a  confusion or a misunderstanding but i  think  it's instructive in that it sort of  reinforces something i've been talking  about for a while which is  if joe biden wins we are getting the  ball back  we are not yet putting any points up on  the board to use a sort of football  analogy  and we're going to have to push joe  biden if he's president and we're going  to have to push him  for the entire time that he is president  so i'm not  hugely worried about this for two  reasons number one  um i i actually do think it was probably  some kind of a mistake or  misunderstanding  because this is not how the dnc would  probably do this  also more than likely if they didn't  plan  to end fossil fuel subsidies or even try  to they would just leave it in but then  just not do it and blame republicans  so i i just i think that that's probably  not the explanation  but either way we are going to have to  as progressive activists hold joe biden  accountable if we want to get things  done and put points on the board if he  indeed becomes president of the united  states  so i don't think this was some kind of  deliberate betrayal by joe biden his  campaign  seems to have been clear the whole time  and by the way i have to tell you  something else on this particular issue  of ending fossil fuel subsidies  it's going to be difficult to do in four  years it's going to be difficult to do  maybe even in eight years  it should be done we should be shifting  subsidies away from fossil fuels and to  renewables but in practice it's going to  be difficult to do it doesn't mean we  shouldn't try but  part of being able to do it is going to  be getting  off of these fuels in the first place  and it is kind of a chicken egg scenario  as we continue to be dependent on fossil  fuels it will be difficult to remove the  subsidies  and if we remove the subsidies it will  be difficult to get off of them because  the prices of fossil fuels will be kept  artificially low  by the subsidies themselves but it's  going to have to be  a sort of step by step by step but the  hot takes  that are saying this is proof of biden  this or  this is proof of biden that  joe biden's climate proposal would be  the most progressive of any president if  biden wins  and either way we are going to have to  hold him  accountable and that will be the mission  of progressive media i hope that's what  i'm anticipating my job to be  for the next four or eight years if joe  biden succeeds at removing donald trump  in november
 

